§ `Section 7: power exercised before commencement`

-- A power to make regulations or do any other thing, in an enactment not yet in force, may be exercised before commencement for
-- the purpose of making it effective on its commencement; what is so made or done has no effect until commencement, except in so
-- far as necessary to make the enactment effective on its commencement.  "In so far as necessary" is the caller's input for the day asked about.
-- src:66 | 7 Where an enactment is not in force and it contains provisions conferring power to make regulations or do any other thing, that power may, for the purpose of making the enactment effective on its commencement, be exercised at any time before its commencement, but a regulation so made or a thing so done has no effect until the commencement of the enactment, except in so far as may be necessary to make the enactment effective on its commencement.
@ref Interpretation Act s 7 (src:66)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the first day the enactment is in force` IS A DATE
      `it is necessary for the thing to have effect on that day to make the enactment effective on its commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a regulation made or a thing done before commencement has effect on` `the day asked about` `where the enactment is first in force on` `the first day the enactment is in force` `and` `it is necessary for the thing to have effect on that day to make the enactment effective on its commencement` MEANS
        `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the first day the enactment is in force`
     OR `it is necessary for the thing to have effect on that day to make the enactment effective on its commencement`

§ `Section 18(3): when a proclamation takes effect`

-- A proclamation issued under an order of the Governor in Council may purport to have been issued on the day of the order or
-- on any subsequent day, and then takes effect on that day.  A day before the order is not one the section allows.
-- src:139 | (3) A proclamation that is issued under an order of the Governor in Council may purport to have been issued on the day of the order or on any subsequent day and, if so, takes effect on that day.
@ref Interpretation Act s 18(3) (src:139)
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the day the proclamation purports to have been issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a proclamation takes effect, issued under an order of` `the day of the order` `purporting to be issued on` `the day the proclamation purports to have been issued` MEANS
    IF   `the day the proclamation purports to have been issued` AT LEAST `the day of the order`
    THEN `the day the proclamation purports to have been issued`
    ELSE `the Act does not say what day a proclamation takes effect if it purports to be issued before the order`

-- src:139 | (3) A proclamation that is issued under an order of the Governor in Council may purport to have been issued on the day of the order or on any subsequent day and, if so, takes effect on that day.
@ref Interpretation Act s 18(3) (src:139): a purported day before the order is not provided for
