§ `Section 30: the day a specified age is attained`

-- A person is deemed not to have attained a specified number of years of age until the commencement of the anniversary, of the
-- same number, of the day of that person's birth.  The anniversary of a day that the anniversary year does not have (29 February,
-- in a year that is not a leap year) is not defined by the text, and section 30 does not send the reader to section 28: it refuses
-- (fork F-30-LEAP).
-- src:234 | 30 A person is deemed not to have attained a specified number of years of age until the commencement of the anniversary, of the same number, of the day of that person’s birth.
@ref Interpretation Act s 30 (src:234)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary of` n `years of the day of birth` b MEANS
    IF   `a count of whole units, at least one` n
    THEN IF   DATE_DAY b AT MOST `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH b) (DATE_YEAR b PLUS n)
         THEN YMD (DATE_YEAR b PLUS n) (DATE_MONTH b) (DATE_DAY b)
         ELSE `the Act does not say which day is the anniversary of a day of birth that the anniversary year does not have`
    ELSE `the Act has no rule for a count that is not a whole number of at least one`

-- src:234 | 30 A person is deemed not to have attained a specified number of years of age until the commencement of the anniversary, of the same number, of the day of that person’s birth.
@ref Interpretation Act s 30 (src:234)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Act does not say which day is the anniversary of a day of birth that the anniversary year does not have` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Act does not say which day is the anniversary of a day of birth that the anniversary year does not have"

-- Deemed not to have attained it until the commencement of the anniversary: on the anniversary itself, from its first moment, it has been attained.
-- src:234 | 30 A person is deemed not to have attained a specified number of years of age until the commencement of the anniversary, of the same number, of the day of that person’s birth.
@ref Interpretation Act s 30 (src:234)
GIVEN b IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      e IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person born on` b `has attained` n `years of age on` e MEANS
    e AT LEAST `the anniversary of` n `years of the day of birth` b

